-- Source module: Solutions.R6Prm
/-!
# Shared parameter record for Jain's round six (`IntMul.Kappa.jain_round6_framework`)

`CrudeAssembly ab ac β ε x C₁ κ mc sc` is stated with real `x, C₁`, arbitrary `ε ∈ (0,1)`
and the savings `ab, ac`.  The normalization `r6_normalize` (file `R6Norm.lean`) turns
it into a `Prm` with

* `τ = 1 - ab`, `σ = 1 - ac` (the bit / complex moment exponents, both in `(0, 1]`),
* `ε ∈ [1/2, 1)` (raising a small `ε` to `1/2` only enlarges the gap),
* natural `x ≥ 1` and natural `C1` (rounded up),
* `lamp` = the `λ'` of `CrudeAssembly` (`lampOf τ σ`).

## Design choice for `lamp`
`Prm.Ok` only requires `lampOf P.τ P.σ ≤ P.lamp` (plus `P.lamp < 1` and the two `ε`-constraints
in terms of `P.lamp`).  So downstream workers may use `D ^ P.lamp` as an *upper* exponent for
every cost term that `CrudeAssembly` bounds by `D ^ λ'` (in particular `lamp ≥ τ, σ, χ, leaf`
with the `10⁻¹⁶` slacks: see `Prm.Ok.tau_lt_lamp`, etc.).  `r6_normalize` produces
`lamp = lampOf τ σ` exactly, but no downstream proof should rely on equality.

`β = 1/1000` is fixed (`R6.beta`).  `Prm.gap` is the minimum of the five cost margins of
`CrudeAssembly`; `r6_normalize` gives `κ < P.gap`.
-/

namespace IntMul.Kappa.R6

namespace Prm

theorem gap_le_one_sub (P : Prm) : P.gap ≤ 1 - P.ε := by
  unfold gap; simp only [min_le_iff, le_refl, true_or]

end Prm

end IntMul.Kappa.R6

end

